I LOVED Worms World Party back in the day.
Man, if this game would be just WWP in HD, I would cry rainbows.
Sadly, it is not.
Awful "physics 2.0" of this game include:
worms slipping off high-elevated surfaces in annoying manner;
grenades sticking to worm's head when flying on warp-speed and slipping off when put carefully;
horrible airstrike, where one rocket displaces others on explosion;
increased worm-surface friction - if a worm travels at the speed of light and touches a pixel of a ground, it stops like they are both made of velcro.
Other awesome changes are:
increased knockback where it was fine (remember how cool it was to stomp a worm into the hell with a donkey? Forget it - worm will fly away or stick to the abyss wall due to friction after first donkey punch);
decreased knockback where it was fine, too - sweet dragonballs and fire punches are much less sweet now, prod should be removed at all, and earthquake is very predictable;
decreased weapon damage - dynamite, sheep, old woman, HHG are just not the same fun they used to be. Grenade was always considered to be a more skilled weapon than bazooka - why do they damage equally, then?
ninja rope is very difficult to handle in many cases now;
worms and delayed blast weapons sometimes get stuck in really wide map corners.
no flamethower. seriously, it was awesome weapon;
Overall, I still manage to get certain fun off playing this, but there is still a lot of flaws, and sadly, they are considered to be advantages.

